      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Sheru lived alone in the forest and ate only raw meat every day. One evening, he smelled something wonderful drifting from a village nearby – spices, rice and slow-cooked flavours he had never known. Curious, he crept closer and watched through a window as a grandmother stirred a huge pot of biryani, layering rice and meat with care.\n\nThe next morning, Sheru found the old woman gathering firewood. Instead of running, she looked at him calmly and said, \"If you promise not to scare anyone, I will teach you.\" Sheru nodded. For weeks, she showed him how to wash rice, fry onions until golden, mix spices in the right order and let everything cook on low heat. His paws were clumsy at first, but he learned.\n\nWhen his first biryani was ready, Sheru invited the forest animals to taste it. They were stunned – a tiger who cooked! The flavour was rich and warm, and everyone asked for seconds. From that day, Sheru became famous not for his roar, but for his biryani, and the old woman visited him often to share meals and stories.\n\n4:50 AM",
